course: dictionary
lesson: 11795
title: Kind and gentle words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound grown-up, but you can work them out from the clues around them. Benign is one of these. The words near it show you what it means: kind, gentle and not harmful.
explain: «The old dog gave a benign smile and wagged its tail.» A smile with a wagging tail is friendly, not scary. So benign describes something gentle that does no harm. Check it: put "kind and gentle" in place of benign and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Doctors use benign in a different way. «The doctor said the lump was benign, so it was not cancer.» Here benign means the lump is not harmful and will not spread. It is the same idea of "not harmful", used in a new setting.
fact: Benign means kind, gentle and not harmful.
fact: Benign is a formal word, so you will often meet it in books and in descriptions of people.
fact: In medicine, a benign lump or tumour is not cancer and does not spread.
fact: Benign is the opposite of harmful or dangerous.
fact: A benign smile is a kind, friendly smile.
exercise: «The old dog gave a benign smile and wagged its tail.» What does benign mean here? | Loud and noisy | *Kind and gentle | Very tired | Scary and fierce
exercise: «The doctor said the lump was benign.» What does benign mean in this sentence? | *Not harmful, and not cancer | Growing quickly and spreading | Painful and sore | Very large and heavy
exercise: «The kitten gave a benign purr as it curled up on my lap.» Which clue shows that benign means gentle? | Hissed and ran away | *Purred and curled up | Stomped and shouted | Knocked over a cup
test: «Grandma has a benign face, so the children feel safe.» What does benign mean? | Hungry | *Kind and gentle | Dangerous | Angry
test: Why was the doctor pleased that the lump was benign? | *It was not cancer and would not spread | It was in her leg | It was going to get bigger | It hurt a lot
exam: What is the best way to check the meaning of a new word in a sentence? | Ask someone to read the whole book to you | Guess the longest word in the sentence | Skip it forever and never come back | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
